Z||000000||BlackARROW||05-03-2001||11:09 PM||||Does anyone know the top speed of stock Fiero with the L4 and the V6?  I'd like to know for 1985' models, especially.<P>I know the HP on the L4 increased year by year, probably the same thing about the V6, I'm just wondering for my personnal info.  Any charts?  Links?<P>One thing is sure: the speedometer stops at 85 mph.  Some people should know anyway.<P><BR>Thank you<P><BR>BA-&gt;<BR>Fiero 2M4 '85 (118,000 miles)<p>[This message has been edited by BlackARROW (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||HummelHund||05-03-2001||11:20 PM||||Actually, I believe we agreed that the '85 GT was the fastest of the V6's due to the 140hp that year had. I don't know about the Dukes. Here's the top speeds I found at <A HREF="http://www.supercars.net" TARGET=_blank>www.supercars.net</A>  (Yes, the Fiero is a supercar! Who'd a thunk it?)<BR>1984 Fiero SE 2M4: 103.0 mph<BR>1985 Fiero GT: 125.0 mph<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000002||HummelHund||05-03-2001||11:23 PM||||Oh, and the April '88 issue of Car and Driver gives the Fiero Formula's top speed as 123 mph.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000003||BlackARROW||05-03-2001||11:33 PM||||Thanks a lot.<P>I'll try out some theories then..<P>I know the Fiero is a super car, but not actually a SuperCar (which usually represents cars above the 550 hp).  On those sites, usually they class it as a ConceptCar.  And what a Concept!!  Woooo...<P>Stay Sharp||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||05-03-2001||11:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackARROW:<BR><B>Does anyone know the top speed of stock Fiero with the L4 and the V6?  I'd like to know for 1985' models, especially.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ive had my '85 Sport Coupe over 110 MPH. (The needle was pointed at the first number on the right of the Trip Meter. (The tach was Red Lined)<P>My '88 Formula, 120 MPH (So Far  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">    </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||11
