Z||000007||BlackARROW||05-03-2001||11:49 PM||||Ouch!  That's what I call.. a bad ticket!<P>Maybe you can tell:   at 96 mph, my tach is at 3600 rpm.  I find it very low, don't you?  When I ride casually at 3000 rpm, I'm going at 80 mph.  Tach/tach filter problem or what?  Did someone did a modif with the gearing without telling me?  By calculation, it would mean that at 112 mph, it should be at 4200 rpm (while the yellow is at 4500 and the real red at 5000)  When I think I have an old Duke, looking at those numbers: I wonder.  <P>Have fun - top less  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Master_Sushi||05-03-2001||11:51 PM||||I'm not sure what I've hit in my 88 coupe because of my 85mph Speedo. But I know its well into 100's. I had the Speedo back to 0  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, I would guess low 120s. I have the auto Trans, and it was about 1/2 way in the yellow line(about 4600rpm). This was down the QEW on a quiet weekday morning, no cars in site for miles. Needless to say it wasn't instantly up to that speed, I was floored for a few mins. It didn't feel bad at the speed though, my headlights didn't pop up and the car was still pretty stable.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BlackARROW||05-03-2001||11:55 PM||||Here we go again with that pop-up headlight flaps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Probably it will happen to me when I'll try  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I did a temporary side scoop myself as a test, finding that my motor was rushing for air sometimes... well I'll try that tomorrow around those biggy 90-100 mph... Oooh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Probably it'll be better..  maybe.  I like homemade stuff.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||05-04-2001||12:27 AM||||I had my 86 GT with some light mods to 5400 in 4th gear with close to stock height give or take .2/3"tires , works out to in the neighbourhood of 140mph...<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Thecrewchief1||05-04-2001||02:18 AM||||Mind did 117 going up the Sunshine Skyway.<P> <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/thecrewchief/861-2GT.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/thecrewchief/861-2GT.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||ChadMan||05-04-2001||08:48 AM||||The top speed of my 84 Sport Coupe (4 sp/4:10) was 103, and it was redline limited...I had a little more pedal but didn't want to venture up into the red.<P>The top speed of my 88 Coupe (5 sp) is 108, drag limited.  Pedal on the floor.  It wouldn't go any faster unless I got a nice tailwind (or a push from a V6 Fiero).<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 05-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||05-04-2001||09:26 AM||||An interesting note from that supercars web site:<P>  Lateral acceleration: 0.81 g's !!!<P>  for a base model Porche 911: 0.76 g's!!!<P>  we corner better than a $60,000 porche!<P>    I LIKE it!||||reg||1
